    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d819">

                <pb facs="0990" n="974" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg974"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.20 Missions/3–1947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Paraguay
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-21T19:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Urtel 125 Mar 19 11 a.m.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d819-f1"/> Dept and War concur undesirable cancel military missions
                    contracts. While such unilateral action provided for in present circumstances by
                    art. 5<anchor n="13" xml:id="d819-f2"/> which could be invoked if Paraguayan
                    Government not amenable to temporary suspension of activities, it is believed
                    that immediate agreement between mission chiefs and Commander-in-Chief should be
                    reached under art. 7 (air mission agreement)<anchor n="14" xml:id="d819-f3"/>
                    whereby missions withdraw from active duty during hostilities. War advises that
                        Crittenberger<anchor n="15" xml:id="d819-f4"/> has already cabled <pb
                        facs="0991" n="975" xml:id="pg975"/> orders both missions to cease
                    activities. Please advise status Brazilian and Argentine missions under State of
                    War.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d819-f1" n="12" xml:id="d819-f1-content">
